{"ref":"BDB, סַבָּל","hw":"סַבָּל","html":"† <big><span dir=\"rtl\">סַבָּל</span></big>  <strong>n.</strong>[<strong>m.</strong>] <strong>burden-bearer</strong>, (late);—only abs. <span dir=\"rtl\">ס׳</span> coll. <a data-ref=\"Nehemiah 4:4\" href=\"/Nehemiah.4.4\">Ne 4:4</a>; <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 2:1\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.2.1\">2 Ch 2:1</a>, <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 2:17\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.2.17\">17</a>; mpl. abs. <span dir=\"rtl\">סַבָּלִים</span> <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 34:13\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.34.13\">2 Ch 34:13</a>;—<span dir=\"rtl\">נֹשֵׂא סַבָּל</span> <a data-ref=\"I Kings 5:29\" href=\"/I_Kings.5.29\">1 K 5:29</a> is certainly wrong; 𝔊 αἴροντες ἄρσιν, 𝔙 <em>qui onera portabant</em>, hence prob. <span dir=\"rtl\">נֹשֵׂא סֵ֫בֶל</span>; > <span dir=\"rtl\">אִישׁ סַבָּל</span>, as ‖ <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 2:1\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.2.1\">2 Ch 2:1</a>.","next":"BDB, סִבְלָה","prev":"BDB, סֹ֫בֶל"}